      "type": "spotlight",
      "item": "tribalpower:song_thread",
      "text": [
        "Redstone is a shout; Song Thread is a hummed line through the air. It carries a signal from **0 to 15** in all **six directions**, up and down included, and needs nothing to rest on."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Running a line",
      "text": [
        "Power drops by **one per block**, like dust. Keep a line short if you need a full 15 at the far end, or refresh it with an Echo plate.",
        "Vanilla dust, levers, song plates, Song Vines and comparators all speak to it.",
        "It carries weakly: it will not power the stone it touches, so it never latches. A wall of thread is a wall of song. For a tendril that hugs stone around corners, see [Song Vine](song_vine)."
      ]
    },
