    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Keeping time",
      "text": [
        "A Drumheart counts beats **17 to 23 ticks** apart as on time, worth **24 Pulse**. Faster pulses earn less, and beats under 8 ticks apart are ignored, so a steady one-second Heartbeat lands every beat.",
        "If the drum does not fill, check the plate's facing, its support block and the thread, and remove any constant power nearby. Get the clock and drum working before you add thresholds or memory plates.",
        "Add a [Pulse Gauge](pulse_gauge) if you want the stored amount as a signal."
      ]
